/A 1367 0 R
/Alt (The flowchart illustrates a three step local context aware modelling and spatial prediction process. Step 1, Identifying local outliers, begins with a Target variable represented by a diamond with circles, and Covariates as a diamond. An arrow from Target variable points to a stacked diamond shape labelled Positive outliers and Negative outliers. An arrow from Covariates also points to this stacked diamond. Step 2, Feature based spatial stratification, shows three boxes: Spatial K means clustering, Gaussian mixture model GMM, and Spectral clustering. An arrow from these boxes points to a diamond labelled Feature based spatial strata. An arrow from the stacked diamond in Step 1 and an arrow from Feature based spatial strata in Step 2 both point to a box labelled Spatial overlay and binding all variables. An arrow from this box points to Step 3, Local context aware modelling and spatial prediction. Step 3 shows a diamond with internal divisions, leading to three irregular shapes. Each irregular shape has an arrow pointing to a Local model A, B, or C box, which then points to a Local prediction using model A, B, or C box. These three prediction boxes converge with arrows to a final diamond labelled Spatial predictions.)
/K 17
/P 35 0 R
/Pg 14 0 R
/S /Figure
/Type /StructElem
>>
