/A 1425 0 R
/Alt (The heatmap displays correlation coefficients between precipitation and selected explanatory variables and outliers. The horizontal axis lists Precipitation, Elevation, Evaporation, Surface runoff, Wind speed, Positive outlier of Elevation, Positive outlier of Evaporation, Positive outlier of Surface runoff, Positive outlier of Wind speed, Negative outlier of Positive outlier of Elevation, Negative outlier of Evaporation, Negative outlier of Surface runoff, Negative outlier of Positive outlier of Elevation, Negative outlier of Evaporation, and Negative outlier of Positive outlier of Wind speed. The vertical axis lists the same variables in the same order. The grid cells show correlation values ranging from 1.0 to minus 1.0, indicated by a colour scale on the right, where red is positive, blue is negative, and white is near zero. Cells marked with an X indicate a non-significant correlation. Many cells contain the text nan, indicating not a number. The diagonal from top left to bottom right is not filled. The heatmap shows varying degrees of correlation and non-significant relationships across the variables.)
/K 7
