/Alt (The four panel heatmap arranged two by two displays precipitation in millimetres across a geographical region. Panel a, labelled Machine learning, shows a distribution with lower precipitation, indicated by lighter blue, in the upper left and central areas, transitioning to higher precipitation, shown in red and orange, in the lower right. Panel b, labelled Machine learning with local outliers, presents a similar pattern to panel a, with lower precipitation in the upper left and central areas and higher precipitation in the lower right. Panel c, labelled Spatial context-aware machine learning, also shows a comparable distribution, with lower precipitation in the upper left and central areas and higher precipitation in the lower right. Panel d, labelled LOCA, exhibits a consistent pattern of lower precipitation in the upper left and central areas and higher precipitation in the lower right. All panels share a common legend indicating precipitation from 100 to 800 millimetres, with blue representing lower values and red representing higher values.)
