/Alt (The line graph displays four models precipitation predictions in millimetres on the vertical axis against longitude in degrees East on the horizontal axis. The horizontal axis ranges from 89.0 degrees East to 97.0 degrees East. The vertical axis ranges from 0 to 600 millimetres. The four models are represented by different line styles: Machine learning is a solid blue line, Machine learning with local outliers is a dashed green line, Spatial context-aware machine learning is a dotted purple line, and LOCA is a dash dot red line. All four lines generally follow similar trends, showing multiple peaks and valleys across the longitude range. An inset map in the upper left corner shows a geographic outline with a dashed line indicating the cross section from northwest to southeast.)
