/A 1451 0 R
/Alt (The six-panel scatter plot, arranged in two rows of three, compares predicted versus observed precipitation in millimetres. Each panel shows a diagonal dashed line representing perfect agreement. Panels a, b, and c represent K-means-stratified ML, GMM-stratified ML, and Spectral-stratified ML respectively. Panel a shows an R squared value of 0.761. Panel b shows an R squared value of 0.760. Panel c shows an R squared value of 0.764. Panels d, e, and f represent K-means-stratified context-aware ML, GMM-stratified context-aware ML, and Spectral-stratified context-aware ML respectively. Panel d shows an R squared value of 0.797. Panel e shows an R squared value of 0.791. Panel f shows an R squared value of 0.779. All horizontal axes are labelled Observation of Precipitation in millimetres, ranging from 0 to 800. All vertical axes are labelled Prediction of Precipitation in millimetres, ranging from 0 to 800. The data points are scattered around the diagonal line in all panels, indicating a positive correlation between observed and predicted values. The R squared values are higher for the context-aware models in the bottom row, suggesting improved prediction accuracy.)
/K 5
/P 35 0 R
/Pg 23 0 R
/S /Figure
/Type /StructElem
